---
// Draft: the Sublime agents case study on an unlinked, unindexed preview route. Move it onto its live slug only when Patrick says to.
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/icons/Icon.astro';
import { ArrowLeft01Icon } from '@hugeicons/core-free-icons';
import HeroRule from '@/components/sublime/HeroRule';
import MessageDetail from '@/components/sublime/MessageDetail';
import JobReview from '@/components/sublime/JobReview';
import AutoAccepted from '@/components/sublime/AutoAccepted';
import AutomationConfig from '@/components/sublime/AutomationConfig';
import AdeJobs from '@/components/sublime/AdeJobs';
import AdeSetup from '@/components/sublime/AdeSetup';
import Coverage from '@/components/sublime/Coverage';
import Lessons from '@/components/sublime/Lessons';
import '@/components/query-builder/query-builder.css';
import '@/components/case-study/case-study.css';
import '@/components/sublime/sublime.css';

const title = 'Closing detection gaps as fast as new threats appear';
const description = 'I designed how Sublime’s agents turn a missed threat into a detection rule, cutting time to coverage while customers stay in control.';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} noindex>
  <article class="qb-page qb-case sb">
    <nav class="qb-case-nav" aria-label="Case study navigation">
      <a href="/work"><Icon icon={ArrowLeft01Icon} size={16} />Work</a>
    </nav>

    <header class="qb-slide qb-hero">
      <p class="qb-company"><img src="/images/logos/square-sublime.svg" width="30" height="30" alt="" />Sublime Security</p>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p>I designed how Sublime’s agents turn a missed threat into a rule, while customers stay in control.</p>
      <dl class="qb-brief">
        <div><dt>When</dt><dd>2025 to now</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Staff Product Designer</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Team</dt><dd>Sublime design team</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Outcome</dt><dd>&lt; 2 hr average time to coverage</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <HeroRule client:load />
    </header>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="problem">
      <h2 id="problem">Every missed threat became detection engineering work</h2>
      <p>A malicious verdict with no matching rule meant a trip to the Rule Editor, and hours of writing and testing by hand.</p>
      <MessageDetail variant="gap" client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="setup">
      <h2 id="setup">Introduce the agent before asking for trust</h2>
      <p>From the hub, ADÉ’s page explains the loop it runs, and how fast, before anything is turned on.</p>
      <AdeSetup client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="handoff">
      <h2 id="handoff">Hand the miss to ADÉ where you find it</h2>
      <p>One click beside ASA’s verdict starts a job, and the job page shows ADÉ at work.</p>
      <MessageDetail variant="handoff" client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="bet">
      <h2 id="bet">The agent hands over work people can read and own</h2>
      <p>A black‑box agent hides its logic. ADÉ puts its intelligence into a detection rule in MQL that your team can read, edit and deploy at scale, so people and the agent work on the same thing.</p>
      <JobReview client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="efficacy">
      <h2 id="efficacy">Let the backtest decide how much review a rule needs</h2>
      <p>Every recommendation carries its hunt result. When the match clears your threshold, the rule goes live on its own.</p>
      <AutoAccepted client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="trust">
      <h2 id="trust">Trust in autonomy has to be earned</h2>
      <p>Teams choose, per verdict, when ADÉ starts on its own and when it can accept its own rules.</p>
      <AutomationConfig client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="outcome">
      <h2 id="outcome">Design the on‑ramp, not the chat</h2>
      <p>Agents work out of sight, so ADÉ’s page shows its impact and every job it starts, for teams to watch and steer. All of it has shipped or is shipping.</p>
      <AdeJobs client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="result">
      <h2 id="result">Missed threats are covered in under two hours</h2>
      <p>Time to Coverage is ADÉ’s headline number: from a missed threat reaching ADÉ to a rule ready to accept. Across customers, it averages under two hours.</p>
      <Coverage client:visible />
    </section>

    <section class="qb-slide" aria-labelledby="lessons">
      <h2 id="lessons">What the agents taught me</h2>
      <Lessons />
      <p class="sb-footnote">Product screens are recreated in code from Sublime’s design prototypes. Figures in them are sample data, except the under‑two‑hour time to coverage.</p>
    </section>

  </article>
</PageLayout>
